{"id":466,"flavor":[{"games":["Legends: Arceus"],"text":"Its evolution was induced by an unusual item, and its electrical output rises along with its heart rate. From its tails, it can unleash an electric current measuring 20,000 volts."},{"games":["Shield"],"text":"In terms of electrical-energy output, Electivire is one of the best among all Electric Pokémon. It discharges high-voltage currents from its tails."},{"games":["Sword"],"text":"The amount of electrical energy this Pokémon produces is proportional to the rate of its pulse. The voltage jumps while Electivire is battling."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"A single Electivire can provide enough electricity for all the buildings in a big city for a year."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"It grips its tail, which spews electricity, and then beats down opponents with the power of its electrified fist."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"When it gets excited, it thumps its chest. With every thud, thunder roars and electric sparks shower all around."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"It pushes the tips of its tails against its foes and then lets loose a high-voltage current. Its foes are burned to a crisp in an instant."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Y","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"It pushes the tips of its two tails against the foe, then lets loose with over 20,000 volts of power."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","X","SoulSilver","HeartGold"],"text":"As its electric charge amplifies, blue sparks begin to crackle between its horns."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2"],"text":"The instant it presses the tips of its tails onto an opponent, it sends over 20,000 volts of electricity into the foe."},{"games":["White","Black","Platinum"],"text":"Heedless of enemy attacks, it closes in, shoves its tails onto the foe, then looses high voltage."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Motor Drive","hidden":false,"description":"The Pokémon takes no damage when hit by Electric-type moves. Instead, its Speed stat is boosted."},{"name":"Vital Spirit","hidden":true,"descrip